pocketbase JS SDK — vendored copy
=================================

version : 0.26.5
file    : pocketbase.umd.js
size    : 39071 bytes
md5     : 2b7f59d021d818a7ec0e7abf5f144616
source  : https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pocketbase@0.26.5/dist/pocketbase.umd.js

Why this file exists
--------------------
The SDK is vendored (no package.json / build step here) and the UMD bundle
carries no version string, so the copy on disk was unidentifiable — we could not
tell which release it was, whether it was patched, or whether it needed a
security update. The version above was recovered by checksum-matching against
upstream releases on 2026-07-25.

Keep this file next to the SDK and update BOTH together.

To update
---------
  V=0.27.0   # check https://www.npmjs.com/package/pocketbase for latest
  curl -fL "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pocketbase@$V/dist/pocketbase.umd.js" -o pocketbase.umd.js
  md5 -q pocketbase.umd.js    # (md5sum on Linux) — record it above with the new version

Notes
-----
- The JS SDK versions independently of the PocketBase server; 0.26.x talks fine
  to the v0.39.x servers the platform runs.
- The same byte-identical copy is vendored in live-board, fitbase and
  app-template. Update them together or they will drift apart.
